 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Let $D_+(at)=\\operatorname{Spec}(R_a)$ be a standard chart of the first\nblow-up, where $R_a=A[\\mathcal I/a]$ and $a\\in\\mathcal I$. The extended\nideal of $\\mathcal J$ is, by definition, the image of $\\mathcal J$ in\n$R_a$. The equation\n$Z'=\\operatorname{Proj}(\\mathcal A/\\mathcal F\\mathcal A)$ says that its\nideal on this chart is generated by all fractions $f/a^d$ with\n$f\\in\\mathcal F$ (and their $R_a$-multiples). The chart calculation for\nthe exceptional ideal gives $\\mathcal I_E R_a=(a)$. Therefore, for every\ngenerator $f\\in\\mathcal F$,\n\n$$\nf=a^d\\,(f/a^d)\\quad\\text{in }R_a,\n$$\n\nand hence\n$(\\mathcal J\\mathcal O_{X'})R_a=(a)^d\\,\\mathcal I_{Z'}R_a$.\nThis proves the asserted equality on every standard chart. On the overlap\nof the $a$- and $c$-charts one has\n$f/a^d=(c/a)^d(f/c^d)$ and $(a)^d=(a/c)^d(c)^d$; the two products are\nliterally the same ideal after localization. The standard charts cover\n$X'$, so equality of the quasi-coherent ideals glues to\n$b^{-1}\\mathcal J\\,\\mathcal O_{X'}=\\mathcal I_E^d\\mathcal I_{Z'}$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
